{
  "set": "heldout-v1",
  "provenance": "The subscriptions example's fourteen change sets (examples/subscriptions/changes), written before the investigator's first live run for the Action's tests, on a schema no investigator prompt, tool description or test names. Eight fault patterns come from publicly documented incidents, linked in examples/subscriptions/README.md; the implementations, the rubrics and the fault markers are the author's. The rubrics and markers below were written on 2026-11-19, before any model had seen a case.",
  "reading": "The evaluator's manifest. A model reads none of it: the archive it reads holds only the blinded migrations. rubric: every group must match one term in an answer's text. fault_markers: text of the statements at fault; the grader derives their lines in the blinded revision.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "case_id": "held-01",
      "change": "plan-catalog",
      "kind": "clean",
      "origin": "authored",
      "family": "clean control: a table split with a moved foreign key"
    },
    {
      "case_id": "held-02",
      "change": "money-columns-float-roundtrip",
      "kind": "fault",
      "origin": "sourced",
      "family": "a round trip through binary floating point loses a cent",
      "rubric": [["float", "double precision", "floating", "binary"]],
      "fault_markers": ["::float8 * 100"]
    },
    {
      "case_id": "held-03",
      "change": "period-session-timezone",
      "kind": "fault",
      "origin": "sourced",
